// classes can also use this design when a unit or units are brought in" · "we can use this setup while we're planning it to make sure that we
// can pull in any unit and turn it into any kind of class" · the build: "lets get these built". INERT unless ENVSITE's envEdition() says
// "envirothon": every function returns at once otherwise, so Howe, DeWalt and Burris boot byte-identically (test_env_site.js, test_cp_unit.js),
// and Lincoln's Envirothon (ENVUNIT, ENVTEST, ENVIDFLASH, ENVMIRROR in Howe) runs exactly as before.
//   · THE REGISTRY — window.HoweUnits[<unitId>] = {unit, tests, …}: a unit's compiled file registers itself there (units/<id>.js, written by
//     units/build/compile_unit.js). NC Envirothon keeps its own file, envirothon.js, and window.HoweEnvirothon stays as the ALIAS of
