// CPSUGGEST_START — 💡 SUGGESTIONS ON 📅 PACE, THE LIVE MATCHER FOR HER OWN QUESTIONS, THE LINKED CARDS ON EACH ITEM-ANALYSIS ROW
// (DESIGN_class_platform_2026-10-28.md §8.4, §6.3, §6.4, §8.3, §8.6, §9, §13 row 16, §14; PR 16 of the class platform; her yes to building the
// design 2026-10-28). Her words 2026-10-28: "a pace target that gives her all the data and can manipulate things where she can see where
// kids need to be and also kind of help her know what she needs, questions to take out, etc." INERT unless the Envirothon site's console
// is on (envcOn): Howe, DeWalt and Burris never reach a line of it, and Lincoln's app never opens the console.
//   · 💡 SUGGESTIONS, under 📅 Pace's student table (CPPACE's cpSuggestHtml hook): at most 8, the most useful first, each from data the
//     console already has. EVERY ONE IS ONLY A SUGGESTION. **Do it** opens the same control, filled in, and she confirms there; **Not now**
//     saves classes/<cid>/dismissed/<id> = {by, ts, t} so it doesn't come back (↩ Bring back, under "Set aside", takes it off again).
//     Nothing ever changes by itself.
//       nocore  "Q7 (Forestry check-in): 0 of 7 right, and no core card covers it": 3+ answers, 40% or fewer right, and no core card is
//               linked. The linked cards always show, because the match is automatic. Do it → 📝 Tests opened at that question.
//       notest  "384 Wildlife ID cards are not core and on no test": one section's cards of one kind, not core, not hidden, and linked to
//               no question on any of the class's forms. Do it → what hiding them buys, from the planner, BEFORE she confirms (the core
//               finish, the minutes a day, the day the last new card comes), then 🙈 Hide them = ONE multi-path update of classCards (PR 10).
//       miss    "Wildlife and Aquatics can't make 95% by State at 5 a day": the what-if plan misses the target in a section. Do it → the
//               plan's own fix on the bar as a what-if (Try N a day; Core only when Core first is off). Only Save this plan saves it.
//       student "Jonah T. needs 26 new cards a day (~75 min) and gets 5": a student short (or ⚠ on minutes) in the table. Do it → that
//               student's own New cards a day, as a what-if, with their row open.
//       weak    "“Cambium” is missed by 3 of 8": a core card in many students' weak lists. Do it → the card open in 📚 Cards (check the back).
//       easy    "Q3 (Forestry check-in) is right for almost everyone: 7 of 7": 3+ answers, 90% or more right, and the same question is on a
//               separate final. Do it → 📝 Tests at the final's question (she takes it out there, or leaves it).
//     🔒 CPLOCKS: a suggestion whose control is locked for the teacher (cpLockRO tests / cards / plan, or Adrienne's New cards a day lock)
//     shows "🔒 set by <name>" in place of Do it.
//   · THE LIVE MATCHER (§8.4: "For a question the teacher adds, the console runs the same matcher live and lets her tick the right cards").
//     cpSuggestMatch is compile_unit.js's questionLinks rule for one question: a term's front or an ID card's item, as whole words (4+
//     characters), in the question or the keyed answer; a fact whose back holds the keyed answer (or the answer holds the back); a card of
