//   · THREE LEVELS, never more (§6.0): the unit's section (Station) → its Key Concept (terms and facts together, T / F tag on each row) or,
//     for cards with an `item` (ID), 🔎 ID → the item (species) → the card rows, FRONT ONLY. A row inside an item drops "<item> · ".
//   · FOLDED, ONE OPEN AT EACH LEVEL: on first open she sees the section lines and nothing else. Opening a section folds the one that was
//     open; opening a Key Concept or item folds the last; opening a card folds the last card. Moving on folds back what she left, and a
//     folder's "show more" starts again at 20.
//   · COUNTS on every header, after the filters: cards (or "78 of 90 cards") · ⭐ core (shown when not 0). A section with nothing matching
//     drops out. ✎ / 🙈 / ＋ counts come with editing (PR 10).
//   · 20 ROWS AT A TIME per folder ("Show 20 more · N left"); search shows 30 at a time.
//   · SEARCH across fronts, backs, info and sources, every section: one flat list, each row with its path above it, the match marked.
//   · CHIPS: All / Terms / Facts / ID (each only when the unit has that kind) · ⭐ Core only · Not on any test (§8.4's question → card links:
//     compile_unit.js works them out into units/<id>/LINKS.json and the unit's file carries them on each question as `cards`).
//   · AN OPENED CARD: the back in a box, the info line, ⭐ Core / Not core · deck · item · Source · "On the tests: Forestry check-in Q3" (or
//     "On no test question"), and its first photo with its credit when the unit's picture index has one (envirothon/pics, ENVIDFLASH).
