// the teacher (her class) or Adrienne (the unit), and every trim can be put back. INERT unless the Envirothon site's console is on (cpceOn):
// Howe, DeWalt and Burris never reach a line of it, and Lincoln's Envirothon in Howe is untouched (test_cp_trim.js).
//   · WHERE: a ✂️ Trim chip in 📚 Cards (one guarded line in cpcsChipsHtml); while it is on, the list area is the Trim view (one guarded line
//     at the top of cpcsListHtml). The groups, folded like everything else, one open at a time:
//       1 A skill replaces it (one row per skill, its 🔒 reason until it is live) · 2 Rule A one card per front · 3 Rule B catch-all facts
//       · 4 Rule C ID attributes · Rule D ✏️ Shorten (long backs) · ✂️ Trimmed so far (↩ Put back one, or a whole step by its `why`).
//     Each group has its reason text, "Accept this group" (one inline confirm, ONE write) and, on every card, Accept (✂️ Make optional or
//     🙈 Hide) and Skip. Cumulative and never counting a card twice: a card an earlier step takes is not offered again later.
//   · TRIM 1 IS ALREADY IN THE UNIT (PR #163, 2026-10-28: rules A, B, C as core:false in unit.json; PR #172 put 32 back the same night: the 5
//     trees left with no core card and the 27 Wildlife "· class" cards). The view reads the unit as it is today, so those 211 − 32 = 179 cards
//     are counted once, as "already optional in the unit", never offered again. This block changes no card in unit.json.
//   · THE GUARDS (her rules after Trim 1, 2026-10-28), shown on the card in words, checked again on every accept:
//       – an ID item (a tree, an animal, a macro…) is never left with no core card: its last core card can't be trimmed;
//       – a card on a test (the question → card links, §8.4) is trimmed only once the skill that replaces it is LEARNED by the class (4 in 5 of
//         the students with a summary), and then one card at a time with its ⚠; a card on a test that no skill replaces stays in;
//       – a picture card (an ID card; the "· class" cards too) is never in "Accept this group": it needs its own Accept;
//       – a skill's cards are offered only once the skill is LIVE: in the unit, not hidden for the class, its item type built, and its
