// CPPHOTOUP_END
// CPSKILL_START — 🧩 THE SKILL ENGINE: practice that isn't a card, for any unit (DESIGN_class_platform_2026-10-28.md §4.1b, §9, §12,
// §13 row 25; RESEARCH_envirothon_skills_2026-10-28.md §2–§3; PR 25 of the class platform; her yes to building the design, 2026-10-28).
// The research's finding: about 1 Area question in 4 needs a SKILL (read a chart, use a table, fill a worksheet, label a picture, name a
// picture), not a recall card, and knowing the card's facts still doesn't make the worksheet come out right — the traps are steps. This is
// the ENGINE only; each item type (chart, table, sheet, label, id, scale, mock) is its own later PR and registers itself with
// cpSkillTypeAdd from its own block. INERT unless ENVSITE's envEdition() says "envirothon": every function returns at once otherwise, so
// Howe, DeWalt and Burris boot byte-identically, and Lincoln's mirror publishes exactly the summary it did (cpSkillSummary → null there).
//   · unit.skills — a unit lists skills next to its decks: {key, section, type, label, core, steps, data, tests, replaces} (§4.1b). They are
//     read from the unit's catalog entry (CPU_UNITS / units/<id>/index), else from its loaded file (HoweUnits[id].unit.skills). A skill key
//     may hold a "." (soils.triangle); as a database key every "." becomes ":" (cpskFb). Nothing in the shape is Envirothon-specific.
//   · THE THREE STAGES (the worked-example research, §2A / §3.3): 👀 Watch it — a worked example, each step lit up in turn · ✍️ Finish it —
//     the app does the early steps, the student the last ones, and each right round hands over one more step · 💪 On your own. The stage
//     moves up after two right in a row and back one after two misses in a row. Every try is a NEW problem, made from the skill's data.
//   · WHICH STEP WAS MISSED: a try saves the first step that went wrong as a miss code (count:individuals, group:g2, math, range …), never
//     just ✗. That is what makes it teachable (§3.3): the student sees the step, the teacher's Skills fold shows the most-missed step.
//   · THE LEARNED RULE: 4 of the last 5 solo tries right (a try that opened the help chart isn't solo), the right ones on 2+ days, the last
//     one right. Then a review try comes back about 7 days later, then every 14; a missed review un-learns it until it's right again.
//   · ONE WRITE PER SITTING (ID Flash's rule): a sitting is up to CPSK_SITTING tries of one skill, kept in memory; at the end ONE multi-path
//     update on the family instance's mastery: <kid>_skills/<unitId>/<skillKey> = {stage, fade, up, down, learned, at, next, rev,
//     tries:[last 8 {ok, miss, step, secs, help, s, at}], miss:{<code>:n}} and studyLog/<kid>/skills/<yyyymmdd> (its own sid, like
//     "idflash", so the 🌿 session's "Done today" is untouched). Demo: a "would update" toast · ?dryrun=1: nothing.
//   · summary.skills.<section> = {learned, total, miss:{<skillKey>:{<code>:n}}, stage:{<skillKey>:"new"|"shown"|"faded"|"solo"|"learned"}}
//     joins what the mirror publishes (envSummary's one guarded line), so the console, the parent page and the pace see it. Counts and
//     codes only.
//   · HOOK POINTS for later PRs: cpSkillFoldHtml(students) — the Skills fold of ⚠ Most missed (PR 18): skills ranked by % of the class
//     learned, each with its most-missed step · cpSkillPaceLine(summary, section) — "skills learned 2 of 4" beside the core cards in
//     📅 Pace (PR 8) · cpSkillQuestionLine(qid, students) — "4 students haven't learned Biotic index" for the item analysis · CPSK_COST — the
//     planner's fixed cost per skill. Until those land, the line shows on every station row (Scores, the parent page, the student page) and
//     the fold sits under 🏫 Class setup ▸ 🧩 Skills.
//   · ▶ TRY IT (2026-11-10): cpSkillTryOpen(fb) in 🏫 Class setup ▸ 🧩 Skills opens a skill's 👀 Watch it for the teacher in a read-only overlay
//     (cpSkillTryHtml) — the kid's renderer on a tryIt run: nothing recorded, nothing written, dry-run safe.
//   · classSkills/<cid>/<skillKey> = {hide:true} | {core:bool} (+ by, ts) — the teacher's layer, like classCards: her class only, never the
//     unit. 🏫 Class setup ▸ 🧩 Skills: Hide / Show again, Make optional / Make core, and per section "the final waits for the core skills
//     too" = classes/<cid>/plan/<key>/skillsForFinal (default off, [?] Q38). When it is on, the final doesn't open by itself until the
//     section's core skills are learned as well (envtStatus' one guarded line; the line under the station says which).
//   · THE SAMPLE (the demo only, CPSK_DEMO_SKILL): the biotic index worksheet of the research §4.3 — a random sample of kinds, some seen more
//     than once; count KINDS, not animals, in each group; × 3 / 2 / 1; add; pick the rating (Excellent 23+, Good 17–22, Fair 11–16, Poor
//     0–10). It runs on a minimal `sheet` maker for "tally" worksheets (a count per group × a weight, a total, a rating band) — any
//     count-and-weigh sheet in any unit has that shape; the full `sheet` type is its own PR. Skills don't wait for a section's check-in.
const CPSK_SITTING=6, CPSK_KEEP=8, CPSK_SOLO_LAST=5, CPSK_SOLO_NEED=4, CPSK_DAYS_NEED=2, CPSK_UP=2, CPSK_DOWN=2, CPSK_REVIEW_DAYS=[7,14], CPSK_SID="skills";
const CPSK_STAGES=["shown","faded","solo"];
