// CPITEMGEAR_START — 🧰 GEAR AND TOOL PICTURES: the first real skill item type (DESIGN_class_platform_2026-10-28.md §4.1b, §6.7, §13 rows
// 25, 26, 29; RESEARCH_envirothon_skills_2026-10-28.md §4.5, ranked #1 "best buy" in §5; her yes to building the design 2026-10-28; built
// 2026-10-29). The research: the station shows a PHOTO of a net or a tool and asks its name or its proper use (2021 Aquatics Q5, Q19; 2022
// Aquatics Q14–16; 2026 Aquatics Q12; 2022 Forestry Q16; 2026 Forestry Q19–20). The tool cards say what a tool does, but the test shows a
// picture and nobody has seen an increment borer — and no card has any aquatic sampling gear but the Secchi disc. INERT off the site
// (cpskOn): Howe, DeWalt, Burris and Lincoln never reach a line of it.
//   · THE DATA is the unit's: units/<unitId>/unit.json `skills`, compiled by units/build/compile_unit.js (rule 8) into the catalog entry
//     (CPU_UNITS), which the skill engine reads first. NC Envirothon: "Forestry tools by picture" (8) and "Sampling gear by picture" (10),
//     the research's two lists. A gear skill is type "id" with data.kind "gear"; each item = {name, use, src, like:[look-alike names],
//     item? (its photo key, when it differs from the name), check? (its use is field practice, not yet in the study documents)}.
//   · A TRY: one item's picture → 1. What is it? (its name among 4, its look-alikes first) → 2. What is it for? (its use among the same 4).
//     Through CPSKILL's three stages: 👀 both answers shown · ✍️ the name is given and the student picks the use, then both · 💪 both, alone.
//     A sitting never shows an item twice, and the items this student missed come first.
//   · THE PICTURE comes from CPPHOTOS' pool only: cpPhotos(item, data.tags) — repo ← unit ← class, main first, a different photo each show
//     (else any photo of the item that isn't a track or skull, so a teacher's untagged photo still counts). Nothing is hot-linked here and
//     nothing is added to the repo. AN ITEM WITH NO PHOTO shows a clear "📷 Photo needed" box with its name, and the try asks only what it is
//     for (a name can't be asked without a picture). The teacher's 🏫 Class setup ▸ 🧩 Skills lists the items that need one (CPSKILL's one
