// CPSENDEARLY_END
// CPAHEAD_START — 📌 THE ASSIGNMENT AND 🚀 GETTING AHEAD on the class site (DESIGN_class_platform_2026-10-28.md, "Adrienne's asks,
// 2026-10-30 (from Brittany)" part 1; touches §6.8 CPSEND, §8 CPSEATS / CPPACE / CPSHARE, §8.12 and the Boards, CPREVIEW's Keep going,
// CPLOCKS). Her words 2026-10-30: "she wanted to be able to pace like what the kids should be doing and send out, but not hold them back.
// So if a kid gets the pace done and wants to do extra or wants to like do the next phase and go ahead, she wants that option available.
// So I guess the pace and what she sends out is kind of like the assignment, but they can always get ahead and study areas also. And I
// think that needs to be reflected in the points." Her picks: (1) ANY section can be opened — more new cards in the sections already sent
// out, and any section not sent out yet, the next one in the unit's order suggested first; its check-in still comes first; (2) ON by
// default — the teacher turns it off for the class or one student, Adrienne can lock it; (3) cards LEARNED beyond the assignment, and only
// after the day's assignment is done, count double on the effort board and add to the team's points, with a 🚀 "ahead" badge.
// INERT unless the class site (ENVSITE's envSiteOn) and the site's own kid (a kid or parent login, or the demo's kid): every hook hands back
// what it was given for Howe, DeWalt, Burris and Lincoln's mirror (his Envirothon in Howe is untouched — the note at the end).
//   · 📌 THE ASSIGNMENT (one line in renderMastStudy, under the check-in): "Today's assignment: N new · M reviews", read off today's own pile
//     and log — the class plan's New cards a day as the overlay hands it to the session (class ← the family's pick ← the student), only what
//     is sent out (a held section gives nothing, and a section opened early gives nothing to the assignment), Reviews a sitting when the class
//     caps it (CPREVIEW: the assignment is one capped sitting; its Keep going stays extra) — and the family's study days (CPCAL: a day that
//     isn't one has no assignment). ✓ once no assignment card is left and something was studied today.
//   · 🚀 KEEP GOING (after ✓): up to max(5, New cards a day) more new cards today — one more day's worth at most, so a keen student can double
//     the pace without burying the next weeks in reviews. The tap writes ONE family-database record, mastery/<kid>_settings/ahead_days/
//     <YYYYMMDD> = {base, shown, extra, n, m, at} (base = new cards already started today) and starts a sitting. While it runs the day's seat
//     limit lifts; on later days the cards started ahead that are still being learned get seats of their own (cpAheadSessions), so the next
//     assignment still fits.
//   · 🔓 STUDY AHEAD (after ✓): every section not sent out to this student yet (or only partly, by Key Concept), the next in the unit's order
//     first ("next up"). A tap writes the student's own early access, students/<sid>/ahead/<section> = {at, by} through envsWrite — the class's
//     send-out never changes — and applies it like a release FOR THAT STUDENT ONLY: one targeted family update clearing the section's decks'
//     cat_hold / cat_open (never setting one), so ENVTEST's check-in comes first exactly as on a real send-out. A section opened early feeds
//     only the 🚀 extra (cpAheadBank, cpAheadFocus), never the assignment or its focus seats; once the teacher sends it out (CPSHARE notes
//     every release record that reaches the app) it is an ordinary section. A live listener re-applies a record made on another device.
//   · THE SWITCH: classes/<cid>/settings/study/getAhead = "on" | "off" (absent = on) in ⚙️ Class settings; students/<sid>/settings/study/
//     getAhead on the student page (the student's own wins; absent = as the class); Adrienne's lock = CPLOCKS's classes/<cid>/locks/getAhead
//     (🏫 Class setup ▸ 🔒 Locks, or the 🔒 on the card) or ENVCLASSSET's settings/locks/getAhead. Off: the 🚀 / 🔓 buttons are gone and the
//     extra stops; early access already opened stays.
//   · THE POINTS (pure: cpAheadNewOn, cpAheadCards, cpAheadSumOf, cpAheadWeek, cpAheadBoards): a card counts when it was started beyond the
//     day's assignment (after that day's 🚀 / 🔓 tap, past `base`) AND it has climbed out of ⭐ learning onto the ladder — a card merely seen
//     never counts. It counts once, on the day it climbed (its last learning day). summary.ahead = {days:{<YYYYMMDD>:n}, total, started}.
//     💪 Effort: + 2 per such card in the last 7 days (it counts double). 🏆 Team: envsGain's meaning stays (gains over each member's own
//     check-in); a separate, labelled 🚀 bonus adds 1 point for every 10 cards a member has learned ahead (the season's total, per member),
//     and the teams rank on gains + bonus. 🚀 on the effort row and the team row.
//   · THE TEACHER: 🚀 on the grid by the name (a section studied early, or cards learned ahead this week); a 🚀 card on the student page (the
//     sections, the counts, the student's switch); 📅 Pace counts a section opened early as should 0 / is = its learned core cards, so it
//     shows as ahead — and when she sends it out it moves to the normal cell, counted once.
//   · Lincoln in Howe: unchanged (cpAheadOn is false for a mirrored kid). For his mirror to follow this: cplnLoad reads
//     students/howe_lincoln/ahead and the two switches, cpAheadOn answers for him (like cplnpSendOn), and his envSummary adds summary.ahead.
const CPAH_MIN_EXTRA=5, CPAH_EFFORT_X=2, CPAH_TEAM_PER=10, CPAH_DAYS=30;
const CPAH_PART={k:"getAhead",icon:"\u{1F680}",what:"getting ahead",means:"whether students may keep going past the day’s assignment and study sections early",ro:"The Getting ahead switch is greyed."};
const _cpah={mine:null,armed:"",css:false};
function cpahSite(){ return typeof envSiteOn==="function"&&envSiteOn(); }
