// the search and the chips stay pinned just under the console's own sticky bar(s)
function cpctStick(){ try{ const t=document.getElementById("cpct-tools"); if(!t) return; let top=0; document.querySelectorAll(".envs-top,.envs-demo").forEach(b=>{ if(getComputedStyle(b).position==="sticky") top=Math.max(top,b.offsetHeight); }); t.style.top=top+"px"; }catch(e){} }
// CPTESTS_END
// CPRESULTS_START — 📊 PER-QUESTION RESULTS AND THE CLASS ITEM ANALYSIS: the teacher sees which questions her class misses, Lincoln included
// (DESIGN_class_platform_2026-10-28.md §6.4, §6.3, §6.4.1, §9, §12 item 4, §13 row 12, §14 Q11 / Q12 / Q18; PR 12 of the class platform; her
// yes to building the design, 2026-10-28). Her words 2026-10-28 (Q18, yes to Lincoln's answers): "it definitely needs to tell her what is
// the most missed questions and also include him, and that way she can come up with review things for class."
//   · THE MIRROR PUBLISHES THE ANSWERS (envSummary's one hook, cprSumAns). summary.tests.<section>.pre gains { ans, formVer }, and
//     summary.tests.<section>.post gains last = { right, n, date, ans, formVer } (the newest final attempt). ans = { questionId: pick } (an
//     index, a sorted list for select-all, -1 for no answer): about 20 small numbers a form. The teacher already reads students/<sid>/summary,
//     so there is no new path and no new rule (§6.4).
//       - A student on the class site: the attempt's own `ans` (PR 11), cleaned (ids of the form's shape, picks as numbers, at most 80).
//       - LINCOLN, through ENVMIRROR in Howe (her yes, 2026-10-28, Q18): his Envirothon check-in and final answers ONLY. His attempts keep
//         today's positional `answers`, so they are read through the version-1 map (§5.3: position → the unit's question id), and only when
//         the record's form name and question count are the unit's form. formVer 0: he takes the unit's form (the class's edits reach him
//         with L2, later; Q21). Only sections of the unit's tests, only that form's question ids, only numbers: nothing from his other
//         subjects, and NOTHING is written into Howe — the hook adds to the summary object the mirror already sends.
//       - No site and no mirror config (Howe today, DeWalt, Burris) → the hook returns at once and the summary is byte-identical.
//   · 📝 TESTS ▸ 📊 CLASS RESULTS (the item analysis, §6.4): a fold above the forms. Inside, one fold per form that has answers (section ·
//     check-in or final, "N took it", "⚠ N missed a lot"), and in it one row per question, MOST MISSED FIRST: the share right and the
//     most-picked wrong choice. Opened: every choice with how many picked it (✓ on the right one), who missed it and what they picked, the
//     same question on the other form ("final 78% (+49)": pre-<n> ↔ post-<n> on a same-form final, else the same wording), and "Go to the
//     question" (opens it in the forms below, to edit or remove). One open at each level; leaving 📝 Tests folds it back (cpctFoldAll's
//     fresh filter object is the sign). Every student of the class counts, students on the Howe Academy app too.
//     The question rows below get a "% right" mark (⚠ when half or more missed it: CPR_LOW).
//   · STUDENT PAGE ▸ 📝 ANSWERS (§6.4): the check-in and the final side by side, one row per question: ✓ or ✗ and the letter picked (the
//     right one in brackets). The same question on both forms shares a row, and "missed on the check-in, right on the final" gets a green ↑.
//     Folded by section, one open. Parents see scores only, never each answer (Q12): nothing here reaches the parent's page.
//   · VERSIONS (Q11: edits allowed, results kept apart by version). An attempt counts toward a question's numbers when it saw the class's
//     current wording (its formVer is at or after her change); one taken on the unit's form before she changed it is scored on the unit's
//     key and shown apart ("N answered an earlier wording"); one on an earlier class wording is counted, not scored.
//   · FOR LATER PRs (names only; nothing here builds them): PR 16 CPSUGGEST draws the linked cards on each row through cpSuggestRowHtml(row, f)
//     (each row carries the question's `cards`); PR 18 CPMISSED reads cpItemAnalysis(summaries, form), cprForms(), cprAll() and cprMostMissed()
//     (every question ranked across the class: the share who missed, then the count). ⚠ Most missed itself is not built here.
//   · THE DEMO: the eight sample students' check-ins and finals get invented answers that add up to their scores (cprDemoSeed, in memory,
//     on the first paint of either view). Writes NOTHING anywhere: no envsWrite, no ref, no listener.
const CPR_LOW=50, CPR_ANS_MAX=80, CPR_PICK_MAX=10, CPR_WHO=24;
const _cpr={open:false,of:null,or:null,so:null,sid:null,fref:null,css:false,seeded:null,memo:null};
